  "main_findings": [
    "Complete present-state A/B/M/tau evidence is not generically sufficient for a structured future target: 10 climate and 10 barrier-restoration binary truth cases remained unresolved even under the complete current-state library.",
    "The complete eight-coordinate parameter library resolved every frozen structured future binary and exact-map target.",
    "Target-specific parameter evidence was strictly cheaper in channel count than exact W1 parameter-world identification for every truth and every transformation in the frozen benchmark.",
    "Full parameter-world identification required a median of five parameter assays, whereas climate binary decisions required at most one, biotic-stress binary decisions at most two parameter assays and barrier-restoration binary decisions at most two.",
    "For climate, every E1-unresolved binary decision had the same canonical one-assay solution: A niche-breadth level.",
    "For biotic stress, complete present-state evidence was sufficient for every E1-unresolved binary decision, and the combined evidence library reduced all 270 unresolved decisions to one additional channel even though parameter-only designs required two assays in 110 truths.",
    "The preregistered S11 dormant climate fiber remained impossible to resolve with any present-state A/B/M/tau measurement but was resolved by one A-level parameter assay."
  ],
  "claim_boundary": [
    "Evidence-channel cardinality is a finite information count, not monetary, logistical, temporal or ethical field cost.",
    "Canonical minimum parameter frequencies are discriminative properties of the frozen finite universe and must not be interpreted as causal importance rankings.",
    "Exact parameter assays are synthetic known-truth evidence channels; real field proxies would require independent calibration.",
    "The result does not imply that present-state measurements are generally inferior to parameter evidence; biotic stress provides the opposite example in this frozen design.",
    "The result does not alter Phase-I through Phase-V or the frozen EOG-WF and first BAM inverse-identifiability manuscripts."
  ]
